{
  "_comment": [
    "Where every module and test file is going in the PR3-PR8 migration, and where it has actually",
    "got to. A test asserts this map covers every module that exists and that every destination",
    "claimed as 'moved' is importable, so a structural move cannot quietly drop a module or leave",
    "two copies behind. `status` is the honest field: 'planned' until the phase runs, 'moved' once",
    "the code lives at `destination`, 'unchanged' when the module stays where it is by design.",
    "`compat_shim` records that the old import path must keep working via a re-export."
  ],
